  "answer": "This has been reported before. Windows Terminal reloads its settings every time the OS keyboard layout changes, whether you use Ctrl+Shift, Win+Space or the taskbar. The reload is what freezes the UI. It is also why the Settings page redraws and your expanded sections collapse. Terminal#11522 tracks this and it is still open. The maintainers consider skipping the settings reload on a layout change, but I found no released fix. Terminal#20103 shows the freeze gets longer when many tabs hold a lot of scrollback, because the reload takes longer and can run twice back to back. For now, you can turn on Windows' 'Let me use a different input method for each app window' option (Per-Window Keyboard Layout). A commenter in #11522 reports this bypasses the problem. You can also reduce the freeze by closing unused tabs and keeping scrollback small. Please add your Terminal version and details to #11522."
 },
